    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32541" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏmāsum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏmassum</span></b> , i, n.
		Gallic; 
				v.
				infra
			, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>bullock's tripe</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): omasum <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόειον κόπεον
				λιπαρὸν τῇ τῶν Τάλλων γλώττῃ</span>, Gloss. Philox.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patinas cenabat omasi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 15, 34</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 45, 70, §
				180</span></i>.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pingui tentus omaso,</span>”
				<i>with his fat paunch</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 5, 40</span></i>
			.</div>
